e/2.11 and 2.12.0+xpu\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nThe regression is caused by commit b3bc797d23f which added qconv_pointwise.tensor variant support. When PT2E quantization produces tensor-typed x_scale/x_zp (x_scale_zp_are_tensors=True path), the new lowering handles them but does not ensure w_zp is properly converted to int32 for the qconv path on XPU (unlike the qlinear path which has explicit dtype conversion at L798-806). Additionally, the TensorMeta construction failure in select_algorithm.py for XPU extern kernels means benchmarking requests get empty metas, potentially causing incorrect algorithm/kernel selection for grouped/depthwise convolutions like those in shufflenet.\n\n## Proposed Fix Strategy\nIn torch/_inductor/mkldnn_lowerings.py qconvolution_unary (L576-637) and qconvolution_binary (L645+), add w_zp dtype validation and int32 conversion similar to the qlinear path (L798-806). Also investigate why TensorMeta.from_irnodes fails for qconv IR nodes on XPU in select_algorithm.py L3282-3283 and either fix the meta construction or ensure the fallback path still produces correct results.\n\n## Target Repository\npytorch\n\n## Action Items\n- [x] 🔍 Issue formatted (Discovery Agent)\n  <details><summary>Discovery log</summary>\n  \n  **[2026-05-18 09:46:39]**\n  **Summary:** On torch 2.12.0+xpu, PT2E (inductor) INT8 quantization of shufflenet_v2_x1_0 on XPU collapses to near-random accuracy (Acc@1 0.090 vs 66.500 on release/2.11). FP32 on the same build is healthy. The regression is in the XPU PT2E INT8 path, likely in the shared mkldnn lowering for weight zero-point handling or extern-choice tensor meta construction.\n  **Failed tests:** \n  **Dependency:** oneDNN\n  **Commit scope:** Regression between release/2.11 and 2.12.0+xpu\n  **Tokens:** model: claude-sonnet-4 | tokens: 40.1K | in: 4 | out: 821 | cache_read: 35.4K | cache_write: 3.8K | cost: $0.0374\n  <!-- agent:discovery-log -->\n  </details>\n- [x] 🧠 Root cause identified (Triage Agent)\n  <details><summary>Triage log</summary>\n  \n  **[2026-05-18 09:49:33]**\n  **Verdict:** IMPLEMENTING\n  **Reason:** Fix is in pytorch inductor lowering code, specifically mkldnn_lowerings.py w_zp handling for qconv on XPU\n\n  **Target Repository:** `pytorch`\n\n  **Root Cause:** The regression is caused by commit b3bc797d23f which added qconv_pointwise.tensor variant support. When PT2E quantization produces tensor-typed x_scale/x_zp (x_scale_zp_are_tensors=True path), the new lowering handles them but does not ensure w_zp is properly converted to int32 for the qconv path on XPU (unlike the qlinear path which has explicit dtype conversion at L798-806). Additionally, the TensorMeta construction failure in select_algorithm.py for XPU extern kernels means benchmarking requests get empty metas, potentially causing incorrect algorithm/kernel selection for grouped/depthwise convolutions like those in shufflenet.\n\n  **Fix Strategy:** In torch/_inductor/mkldnn_lowerings.py qconvolution_unary (L576-637) and qconvolution_binary (L645+), add w_zp dtype validation and int32 conversion similar to the qlinear path (L798-806). Also investigate why TensorMeta.from_irnodes fails for qconv IR nodes on XPU in select_algorithm.py L3282-3283 and either fix the meta construction or ensure the fallback path still produces correct results.\n\n  **Tokens:** model: claude-sonnet-4 | tokens: 670.9K | in: 24 | out: 4.4K | cache_read: 642.2K | cache_write: 24.3K | cost: $0.3497\n  Log: `agent-issue-364-triaging-20260518-094649.log`\n  <!-- agent:triage-log -->\n  </details>\n- [x] 🎯 Triage complete — routed to fix agent (agent:triaged)\n- [ ] 🔧 Fix implemented (Fix Agent)\n  <details><summary>Fix log</summary>\n  <!-- agent:fix-log -->\n  </details>\n- [ ] ✅ Fix verified locally\n<details><summary>Verification log</summary>\n\n<!-- agent:verification-log -->\n</details>\n- [ ] 📋 PR proposed\n- [ ] 👀 Human review\n- [ ] 🎉 PR merged\n\n## Context\nupstream issue: https://github.com/intel/torch-xpu-ops/issues/3489\nInductor lowering phase (agent_category_inductor_phase: inductor_lowering)\nshufflenet_v2_x1_0 is depthwise/grouped-conv heavy and uses channel-shuffle, historically fragile for INT8 conv lowerings.\nLikely root causes: weight zero-point dtype/layout regression in mkldnn_lowerings.py near L763, extern-choice TensorMeta failure in select_algorithm.py L3254, or grouped/depthwise INT8 lowering gap in mkldnn_ir.py.\n\n## Environment\n<details><summary>collect_env</summary>\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n## Original Issue\n<details><summary>Original issue body</summary>\n\n### Summary\nOn `torch==2.12.0+xpu`, PT2E (inductor) INT8 quantization of `shufflenet_v2_x1_0` on XPU collapses to near-random accuracy. The same flow on `release/2.11` reaches Acc@1 66.5 / Acc@5 86.528, and FP32 on the same 2.12.0+xpu build is healthy. This is a regression in the XPU PT2E INT8 path.\n\n### Environment\n- `torch`: `2.12.0+xpu`\n- Python 3.12 (venv at `/workspace/myvenv`)\n- Device: XPU\n- Quant config: default, PT2E flow via `pt2e-accuracy/scripts/modelbench/quant/inductor_quant_acc.py`\n- Dataset: ImageNet ILSVRC2012 val (standard valprep)\n\n### Reproduce\n```bash\n\ngit clone -b main https://github.com/chuanqi129/inductor-tools pt2e-accuracy\n\nACC_CMD="python pt2e-accuracy/scripts/modelbench/quant/inductor_quant_acc.py \\\n         --device xpu --dataset_dir ${DATASET_DIR}"\nm=shufflenet_v2_x1_0\n\n# INT8 (broken on 2.12.0+xpu)\n${ACC_CMD} --model_list "${m}"\n\n# FP32 (healthy, sanity check)\n${ACC_CMD} --model_list "${m}" --is_fp32\n```\n\n### Results\n\n| Build | Mode | Acc@1 | Acc@5 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| release/2.11 | INT8 (default config) | **66.500** | **86.528** |\n| 2.12.0+xpu | INT8 (default config) | **0.090** | **0.482** |\n| 2.12.0+xpu | FP32 | 69.356 | 88.314 |\n\n### Observed log (INT8 run, 2.12.0+xpu, abridged)\n```\nusing ptq\nW0427 05:36:24 torch/_inductor/codecache.py:832] [1/0] pre_grad_custom_pass function does not implement uuid(); falling back to early timing ...\n/workspace/myvenv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch/_inductor/mkldnn_lowerings.py:763: UserWarning:\n  To copy construct from a tensor, it is recommended to use sourceTensor.detach().clone() ...\n  torch.tensor(w_zp_tensor, dtype=torch.int32), name=w_zp.get_name()\nW0427 05:36:28 torch/_inductor/select_algorithm.py:3254] [1/0] Constructing input/output tensor meta failed for Extern Choice\n\nshufflenet_v2_x1_0 int8:  * Acc@1 0.090 Acc@5 0.482\n```\n\n(The two `torchao` `_C_mxfp8.so` / `_C_cutlass_90a.abi3.so` "Failed to load" lines at startup are unrelated CUDA-only artifacts shipped in the wheel.)\n\n### Analysis (PyTorch + torch-xpu-ops code refs)\n\nThe two warnings emitted only on the INT8 path point at the inductor PT2E lowering for XPU, which is shared with CPU via the mkldnn lowerings:\n\n1. **Weight zero-point handling** — `torch/_inductor/mkldnn_lowerings.py` around L763, in the QConv/QLinear PT2E lowering:\n   ```python\n   w_zp_tensor = V.graph.constants[w_zp.get_name()].to(torch.int32)\n   w_zp = V.graph.add_tensor_constant(\n       torch.tensor(w_zp_tensor, dtype=torch.int32),  # <-- triggers the warning\n       name=w_zp.get_name(),\n   )\n   ```\n   The `torch.tensor(<existing tensor>, dtype=int32)` re-wrap is what produces the user-warning, and is the canonical path for `w_zp` on the PT2E flow. A dtype/layout mismatch here would directly corrupt weight quantization math.\n\n2. **Extern-kernel meta construction failure** — `torch/_inductor/select_algorithm.py` around L3254:\n   ```python\n   try:\n       self.input_tensor_meta  = TensorMeta.from_irnodes(self.input_nodes)\n       self.output_tensor_meta = TensorMeta.from_irnodes(self.layout)\n   except Exception:\n       log.warning("Constructing input/output tensor meta failed for Extern Choice")\n   ```\n   On XPU this exception is being swallowed for the quantized extern choice, so algorithm selection proceeds with empty meta and an extern fallback may be picked / dispatched with the wrong layout. This warning does **not** appear on the FP32 run.\n\n3. **`QConvPointWisePT2E` is shared CPU/XPU** — `torch/_inductor/mkldnn_ir.py` (`QConvPointWisePT2E.create` → `_prepare_convolution_fusion_create`, gated by `SUPPORTED_MKLDNN_DEVICES = ("cpu", "xpu")` in `torch/_inductor/utils.py`). The XPU side delegates to oneDNN graph via the kernel name `aoti_torch_xpu__qconv_pointwise_tensor`. Any change in the shared lowering between 2.11 and 2.12 (w_zp dtype/stride, channels-last propagation, grouped-conv handling) would land on XPU even if originally targeted at CPU.\n\n\n\n## Context\nXPU agent skills and instructions are in /home/stonepia/torch-xpu-ops/.github/skills and /home/stonepia/torch-xpu-ops/.github/instructions. Read the relevant SKILL.md before starting work.\nThe skill for this task is: /home/stonepia/torch-xpu-ops/.github/skills/issue-fix/SKILL.md']' timed out after 3600 seconds
